      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes,\nverified locally on the affected device (Xiaomi apollon, MegaFon RU,\nlineage-23.2). Before the patch:\n\n  DataServiceManager: Carrier config changed. Try to bind data service.\n  DataServiceManager: Can\u0027t find the binding package\n\ndumpsys activity services vendor.qti.iwlan showed only\n.QualifiedNetworksServiceImpl and .IWlanNetworkService bound, never\n.IWlanDataService.\n\nAfter applying the equivalent overlay locally (built and pushed as a\nruntime resource overlay carrying the same\nconfig_wlan_data_service_package value, to test without a full\nrebuild):\n\n  DataServiceManager: onServiceConnected: ComponentInfo{vendor.qti.iwlan/vendor.qti.iwlan.IWlanDataService}\n\nand dumpsys activity services vendor.qti.iwlan now lists\n.IWlanDataService as an active bound service alongside the other two,\nconsistently across reboots and Wi-Fi toggles. This is a direct,\nreproducible before/after confirmation that the missing default was\nexactly what prevented the WLAN transport from ever registering.",
